# Code Searchability & Pattern Matching

## Overview

This codebase uses **ast-grep** for structural code search and pattern matching. ast-grep provides semantic search beyond simple text matching, understanding TypeScript/JavaScript syntax.

See [.ast-grep.yml](mdc:.ast-grep.yml) for complete configuration.

---

## Quick Reference

### Common Search Commands

```bash
# Search for specific patterns
sg search 'async function $NAME'         # Find all async functions
sg search 'const $VAR = fetch($$$)'      # Find all fetch calls
sg search 'throw Errors.$METHOD($$$)'    # Find all error throws

# Run specific rules
sg run find-api-endpoints                # Find API endpoint handlers
sg run find-mcp-handlers                 # Find MCP tool handlers
sg run find-database-queries             # Find D1 database queries
sg run find-validation-calls             # Find validation calls
sg run find-sql-injection-risk           # Find potential SQL injection

# Scan all rules
sg scan                                  # Run all rules
sg scan --rule find-console-logs         # Run specific rule
```

### Search by Feature

| Feature | Command | Location |
|---------|---------|----------|
| **API Endpoints** | `sg run find-api-endpoints` | `src/api/routes.ts` |
| **MCP Handlers** | `sg run find-mcp-handlers` | `src/mcp/handlers/*.ts` |
| **Database Queries** | `sg run find-database-queries` | `src/**/*.ts` |
| **Validation** | `sg run find-validation-calls` | `src/api/routes.ts` |
| **Error Handling** | `sg run find-error-throws` | `src/**/*.ts` |
| **Console Logs** | `sg run find-console-logs` | `src/**/*.ts` |

